# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT SHIPPED (P0 → P2 from workspaces/obayashi/04-validate/
# 13-redteam-comprehensive-2026-05-19.md)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

P0 — security:

  payroll.py:
    _audit_payroll helper appends to immutable AuditLogEntry.
    approve_payroll_run, mark_payroll_paid, cancel_payroll_run all
    dual-write + check_rate_limit. P58 + P57 contract honoured.

  employees.py:
    _audit_employee helper for sensitive-field mutations.
    update_employee:
      - Self-mutation guard refuses to mutate
        {salary_monthly, confirmation_status, probation_end_date,
         is_active, reporting_manager_id, employment_type, designation}
        on the caller's OWN employee row (target.user_id == sub).
      - Emits AuditLogEntry per sensitive field changed.
    confirm_employee, extend_probation, terminate_employee all
    invoke _audit_employee with redacted (old → new) diff.

  integrations.py (pre-existing failure resolved):
    xero_disconnect + xero_pick_org now call check_rate_limit
    per B11 contract.

P1 — demo-credibility:

  services/probation.py (new):
    compute_probation_end_date(start, months) → ISO date.
    ensure_probation_end_date_in_payload(payload) → mutates create.
    auto_confirm_due_probations(as_of=None) → daily sweep:
      - Backfills missing probation_end_date from start + months.
      - Flips on_probation → confirmed when elapsed.
      - Writes EmploymentEvent + AuditLogEntry per flip.
      - Idempotent.

  platform.py:
    _register_daily_lifecycle_ticks() registers an asyncio
    background task that invokes auto_confirm_due_probations
    daily. Bounded by ARBOR_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TICKS env flag
    so tests / CI don't fire it.

  Employee create paths (employees._create_employee + auth invite
  accept) now call ensure_probation_end_date_in_payload so every
  new row gets a deterministic probation_end_date.

  services/advisory_domain_classifier.py (new):
    classify_domains(query) → list of detected regulatory domains
    (cpf / employment_act / efma / wsh / tafep / tax_iras).
    Deterministic keyword/regex matching — no LLM.

  agents/advisory_engine.py:
    Pre-classifies the query before the LLM turn.
    Pre-fetches up to 3 KB provisions per detected domain via
    _search_kb_with_fallback.
    Injects them as a system message above the user turn so the
    LLM has grounded context from round 1 (no parametric-memory
    fallbacks).
    Tracked in kb_results_seen so citations populate even when the
    LLM doesn't explicitly call search_kb.
    Returned "domains" is the union of (a) classifier-detected and
    (b) LLM-search_kb invocations.

  components/shell/NavigationSidebar.tsx (web):
    Adds SidebarRole type, requiredRoles on NavItem, canSeeNavItem
    predicate (P49 — predicate not role proxy).
    /admin and /settings/integrations gated to ["owner"] only.
    Every nav group (core / tools / management / bottom) filters
    through canSeeNavItem.

P2 — polish:

  services/headcount.py (new):
    Canonical "active employee" predicate:
      is_active=True AND
      (end_date IS NULL OR end_date > as_of) AND
      confirmation_status != "terminated"
    Surfaces:
      list_active_employees(company_id, as_of, extra_filters)
      get_active_employee_count(company_id, as_of, extra_filters)
      filter_active_employees(rows, as_of)
    Call sites wired:
      strategy.py _employees_for_company
      reports.py turnover_analysis active-branch
      profile.py company_dashboard + workforce_summary

  apps/web/src/app/(dashboard)/goals/page.tsx:
    Defence-in-depth dedupe by goal.id in fetchAll() so a backend
    join that returns duplicate rows can't render twice.

  src/hr_advisory/api/routers/onboarding.py:
    _enrich_assignment now self-heals seed/migration inconsistency:
    status="completed" with percentage<100 or total==0 demotes
    back to "in_progress" (or "draft" when total==0) and writes
    back so the UI never shows "Completed (0%)".

